(168922, 9498, 4514, '<td valign="top">This is a good shot.  If this was in the middle of a game then you did a wonderful job.  You got the main subject in focus and you blurred the rest getting back on defense.  The only thing I can say is the court is tilted a little.  That can cause for static which makes it a bit unattractive.  You used the rule of thirds nicely and the color is very good considering you were in a halogen light Gym.  Was it possible to set you White balance manually?  If not then Bravo.  I am not sure if there is a problem with the whitebalance but if you used auto for it try customizing your WB.  it can make a great diff.</td>', 'This is a good shot.  If this was in the middle of a game then you did a wonderful job.  You got the main subject in focus and you blurred the rest getting back on defense.  The only thing I can say is the court is tilted a little.  That can cause for static which makes it a bit unattractive.  You used the rule of thirds nicely and the color is very good considering you were in a halogen light Gym.  Was it possible to set you White balance manually?  If not then Bravo.  I am not sure if there is a problem with the whitebalance but if you used auto for it try customizing your WB.  it can make a great diff.', '2002-12-10 00:45:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(168923, 9446, 4267, '<td valign="top">not bad.. I would like to see this shot with the panning technique to see which I like better... a stopped merry go round with a blurred foreground might be neat</td>', 'not bad.. I would like to see this shot with the panning technique to see which I like better... a stopped merry go round with a blurred foreground might be neat', '2002-12-10 00:45:47.000000', NULL, 1),
