(169863, 9516, 4514, '<td valign="top">This is intresting and kinda cool.<br/>You will be the first person I use my New Critique Criteria on.  <br/>1. Does the photo fit the theme? (5)<br/>2. Composition; I think the composition here is good.  You may not know it but you <br/>    used a L shape composition here that works very well.  With most portraits <br/>    of females you want to have the body turned.  It is not a straight on torso <br/>    so you did well with that.  You also Turned her head toward the shoulder <br/>    closest to the Cam.  Bravo.  Works very well for Female portraits.  Though not   <br/>    a closeup, you had her eyes closed enough to were you sould not see the <br/>    Sclara of the Eye above or Below the Iris.  (9)<br/>3. Focus;  Everything that needs to be in focus is in focus.  (7)<br/>4. Background:  Since the background is dark and the the subject is lighter,  you <br/>    have a nice contrast here.  (7)<br/>5.Lighting: The lighting here is a bit flat.  Not much contrast on either side of the <br/>   face.  In Portraits, you would like to have just one light visible in the eye.  I see <br/>   two I think.  Since the lighting is a bit Flat I bid a (5) for the lighting.<br/>Overall Score is a 6.5 but I round to 7.<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is intresting and kinda cool.You will be the first person I use my New Critique Criteria on.  1. Does the photo fit the theme? (5)2. Composition; I think the composition here is good.  You may not know it but you     used a L shape composition here that works very well.  With most portraits     of females you want to have the body turned.  It is not a straight on torso     so you did well with that.  You also Turned her head toward the shoulder     closest to the Cam.  Bravo.  Works very well for Female portraits.  Though not       a closeup, you had her eyes closed enough to were you sould not see the     Sclara of the Eye above or Below the Iris.  (9)3. Focus;  Everything that needs to be in focus is in focus.  (7)4. Background:  Since the background is dark and the the subject is lighter,  you     have a nice contrast here.  (7)5.Lighting: The lighting here is a bit flat.  Not much contrast on either side of the    face.  In Portraits, you would like to have just one light visible in the eye.  I see    two I think.  Since the lighting is a bit Flat I bid a (5) for the lighting.Overall Score is a 6.5 but I round to 7. ', '2002-12-11 00:25:30.000000', NULL, 1),
