(170334, 9456, 3459, '<td valign="top">A beautiful image, well composed and exceptionally well lighted.  Outstanding use of exposure.  The title is great as well.  Congrats, well done!</td>', 'A beautiful image, well composed and exceptionally well lighted.  Outstanding use of exposure.  The title is great as well.  Congrats, well done!', '2002-12-11 14:19:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(170336, 9517, 3459, '<td valign="top">Great composition, you have managed to catch that particular moment which makes a flag project a feeling of pride, action, and everything else it stands for.  I especially like the crop, perfect.  Personally, I would add a bit of saturation, but that''s just an opinion.  Excellent job, congrats!</td>', 'Great composition, you have managed to catch that particular moment which makes a flag project a feeling of pride, action, and everything else it stands for.  I especially like the crop, perfect.  Personally, I would add a bit of saturation, but that''s just an opinion.  Excellent job, congrats!', '2002-12-11 14:21:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(170339, 9416, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does the Photo fit the theme? (2)<br/>2)Color:(4)<br/>3)composition(2)<br/>4)Focus(3)<br/>5)Background(3)<br/>6)Lighting(6)<br/>7)Relavancy of the Title(4)<br/> <br/>Overall Score: 3.42 rounded to 3.<br/> <br/>Commentary: Sorry I was harsh on the scoring but had I not used my new method <br/>                      It would have been evan worse.  There seems to be nothing special <br/>                      about this picture.  You tried to be intresting by leaving the photo on <br/>                      its side, and by doing this you made it worse.  Sorry.  That was just  <br/>                      my oppinion.  I gave a 6 on lighting because you used Shaded light<br/>                      on what appears to be a cloudy day.  That is the only thing that you <br/>                      did right here.<br/> <br/></td>', '1)Does the Photo fit the theme? (2)2)Color:(4)3)composition(2)4)Focus(3)5)Background(3)6)Lighting(6)7)Relavancy of the Title(4) Overall Score: 3.42 rounded to 3. Commentary: Sorry I was harsh on the scoring but had I not used my new method                       It would have been evan worse.  There seems to be nothing special                       about this picture.  You tried to be intresting by leaving the photo on                       its side, and by doing this you made it worse.  Sorry.  That was just                        my oppinion.  I gave a 6 on lighting because you used Shaded light                      on what appears to be a cloudy day.  That is the only thing that you                       did right here. ', '2002-12-11 14:27:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(170344, 9295, 3459, '<td valign="top">A very clear, precise, and beautiful image, congratulations!  I especially like the colour, and your use of DOF.</td>', 'A very clear, precise, and beautiful image, congratulations!  I especially like the colour, and your use of DOF.', '2002-12-11 14:35:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(170345, 9444, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does the Photo fit the theme:(6)<br/>2)Color:(5)<br/>3)Composition:(7)<br/>4)Focus:(5)<br/>5)Background:(5)<br/>6)Lighting:(4)<br/>7)Relavancy of Title:(7)<br/> <br/>Overall Score 5.57 rounded to 6<br/> <br/>Commontary:<br/>I do not think this is a bad shot.  I am big on geting as close as possible to the focal point.  I do believe however that there are some limitations to this theory and I personally do not like it used here.  I think to back away a little bit more and get closer to the ground will cause for a more intresting picture.  I could be wrong but that is just my oppinion.  I think your lines are decent because they lead the eye through the photograph.  Decent Job.  :-)<br/></td>', '1)Does the Photo fit the theme:(6)2)Color:(5)3)Composition:(7)4)Focus:(5)5)Background:(5)6)Lighting:(4)7)Relavancy of Title:(7) Overall Score 5.57 rounded to 6 Commontary:I do not think this is a bad shot.  I am big on geting as close as possible to the focal point.  I do believe however that there are some limitations to this theory and I personally do not like it used here.  I think to back away a little bit more and get closer to the ground will cause for a more intresting picture.  I could be wrong but that is just my oppinion.  I think your lines are decent because they lead the eye through the photograph.  Decent Job.  :-)', '2002-12-11 14:36:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(170346, 9520, 3459, '<td valign="top">Very well done, both composition wise and technically.  The lighting definetly deservs applaus.  Good luck!</td>', 'Very well done, both composition wise and technically.  The lighting definetly deservs applaus.  Good luck!', '2002-12-11 14:36:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(170381, 9380, 1664, '<td valign="top">Better depth of field would have improvet the shot.</td>', 'Better depth of field would have improvet the shot.', '2002-12-11 15:44:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(170382, 9416, 1664, '<td valign="top">Strange gravity field here.</td>', 'Strange gravity field here.', '2002-12-11 15:45:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(170386, 9303, 5364, '<td valign="top">I like this, but it makes the leaf appear to be moving fast, which leaves don''t generally do, so to me, it feels a little wrong - my personal bias I guess.</td>', 'I like this, but it makes the leaf appear to be moving fast, which leaves don''t generally do, so to me, it feels a little wrong - my personal bias I guess.', '2002-12-11 15:51:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(170388, 9404, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does the Photo meet the Challenge? 5<br/>2)Color:7<br/>3)Composition:8<br/>4)Focus:6<br/>5)Background:5<br/>6)Lighting:4<br/>7)Relavance of Title in Photo:7<br/> <br/>Overall Score.  6<br/> <br/>Commontary:<br/>I wish the lighiting was a little better toward the back.  The lines of composition move you very nicley through this shot all the way to the back and then out of the frame.  Good job with that.  :-)</td>', '1)Does the Photo meet the Challenge? 52)Color:73)Composition:84)Focus:65)Background:56)Lighting:47)Relavance of Title in Photo:7 Overall Score.  6 Commontary:I wish the lighiting was a little better toward the back.  The lines of composition move you very nicley through this shot all the way to the back and then out of the frame.  Good job with that.  :-)', '2002-12-11 15:53:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(170392, 9532, 3384, '<td valign="top">beautiful.</td>', 'beautiful.', '2002-12-11 16:00:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(170400, 9280, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does it Meet the Challenge Theme? 6<br/>2)Color:5<br/>3)Compositon:5<br/>4)Focus:3<br/>5)Background:5<br/>6)Lighting:4<br/>7)Title Relavance:6<br/> <br/>Overall Score:4.85 rounded to 5<br/> <br/>Commontary:<br/>This was a good idea.  I think one way this could have been made a wonderful photo was by stopping the poeple in motion and let the Merry-Go-Round Blur nicely.  I realize that would have been staged, but that would have Given a better overall score because I would have been able to see things I really look for when Grading.  I look for a photo that I would hang on my wall.<br/> <br/>Overall Score.</td>', '1)Does it Meet the Challenge Theme? 62)Color:53)Compositon:54)Focus:35)Background:56)Lighting:47)Title Relavance:6 Overall Score:4.85 rounded to 5 Commontary:This was a good idea.  I think one way this could have been made a wonderful photo was by stopping the poeple in motion and let the Merry-Go-Round Blur nicely.  I realize that would have been staged, but that would have Given a better overall score because I would have been able to see things I really look for when Grading.  I look for a photo that I would hang on my wall. Overall Score.', '2002-12-11 16:09:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(170407, 9332, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Photo meet the Theme? 6<br/>2)Color:6<br/>3)composition:(4.5)  I will elaborate.<br/>4)Focus:6<br/>5)Background:5<br/>6)Lighting:6<br/>7)Title Relavance:5<br/> <br/>Overall Score:5.5 rounded to 6<br/> <br/>Commentary:<br/>This was a great idea with decent execution.  Personally I would have turned her body in the direction of the roundy round and put her closer to the edge of the picture on the opposite side of the go round direction. Then turn her head  toward the Camera to the point where you can see one ear fully and barley see the other.  This gives direction and the full front shot like this is used in portraits for mainly men.  Since you made this a bit of a Portrait I will comment accordingly.  Never want to show the back of the hands in a portrait.  That adds whats known as static and kills the lines of the shot.  Another thing you want to do is break the wrist.  You almost did that on the hand that is on the bar.  A full front is a difficult shot to compose right.  I would love to see this shot the way I described.  I would bet you would be surprised. <br/></td>', '1)Photo meet the Theme? 62)Color:63)composition:(4.5)  I will elaborate.4)Focus:65)Background:56)Lighting:67)Title Relavance:5 Overall Score:5.5 rounded to 6 Commentary:This was a great idea with decent execution.  Personally I would have turned her body in the direction of the roundy round and put her closer to the edge of the picture on the opposite side of the go round direction. Then turn her head  toward the Camera to the point where you can see one ear fully and barley see the other.  This gives direction and the full front shot like this is used in portraits for mainly men.  Since you made this a bit of a Portrait I will comment accordingly.  Never want to show the back of the hands in a portrait.  That adds whats known as static and kills the lines of the shot.  Another thing you want to do is break the wrist.  You almost did that on the hand that is on the bar.  A full front is a difficult shot to compose right.  I would love to see this shot the way I described.  I would bet you would be surprised. ', '2002-12-11 16:26:55.000000', NULL, 1),
