(170470, 9580, 2158, '<td valign="top">It''s difficult to just this picture when it''s so small.  This size should only be used for pictures with much less detail (in my opinion anyway).</td>', 'It''s difficult to just this picture when it''s so small.  This size should only be used for pictures with much less detail (in my opinion anyway).', '2002-12-11 19:19:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(170488, 9474, 3084, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  8</td>', 'Very nice.  8', '2002-12-11 19:57:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(170493, 9264, 4007, '<td valign="top">I like the subject of the shot, but it doesn\''t really convey any significant motion.  The motion taking place is insignificant.  The shot is a little dark, and putting the subject dead center doesn\''t seem like the best composition for this.  Perhaps if he were at the far right side with the field laid out before him it would be more interesting.  And while I''m sure it was unavoidable, the net hanging in front of him is distracting.  This shot needs some technical improvement, but it has a lot of potential to it.  Good luck to you.  3</td>', 'I like the subject of the shot, but it doesn\''t really convey any significant motion.  The motion taking place is insignificant.  The shot is a little dark, and putting the subject dead center doesn\''t seem like the best composition for this.  Perhaps if he were at the far right side with the field laid out before him it would be more interesting.  And while I''m sure it was unavoidable, the net hanging in front of him is distracting.  This shot needs some technical improvement, but it has a lot of potential to it.  Good luck to you.  3', '2002-12-11 20:11:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(170494, 9349, 4007, '<td valign="top">Great shot, but doesn''t show motion or convey a sense of motion or really have anything to do with motion (dispite the efforts of the title).  3</td>', 'Great shot, but doesn''t show motion or convey a sense of motion or really have anything to do with motion (dispite the efforts of the title).  3', '2002-12-11 20:13:14.000000', NULL, 1),
